── UNKNOWN NAME ────────────────────── E0211_field_without_self.lt:4:29  [E0211]

`name` is a field, which a method reads as `self.name`:

  4 │   fn speak(self) -> str { "{name} barks" }
    │                             ^^^^

A method reaches its receiver's fields through `self`, as `self.x`.

To fix it, write `self.name`:

  4 │   fn speak(self) -> str { "{self.name} barks" }
    │                             +++++
